uros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 7.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 11.4, with a 95% confidence interval of 7.7 to 17.2. December accounts for 2% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 4% of all its works contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 4. Contract [1], for 38,100 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not indicate improper actions. It could reflect market conditions or budget constraints. The statistical pattern alone does not prove wrongdoing without further investigation.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contracts' dates and amounts for consistency. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same needs. Examine if multiple contracts were used to meet a single requirement, which might indicate a strategy rather than a breach.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["d%2Blxh66rGVbIGlsa0Wad%2Bw%3D%3D","pijuulGVYPw%2FbjW6njtWLw%3D%3D","H%2B30EkuglWoeIBJRHQiPkQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}